From: "Claude (SGR dev session)" <claude@sgr-dev.local>
Date: Sat, 29 Aug 2026 12:09:39 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] test(sentiment): cover SentimentScorer (72% -> 100%)

- Add tests/sentiment/test_nlp_scorer.py: 30 tests covering
  sgr/sentiment/nlp_scorer.py's SentimentScorer.
- _initialize() backend-selection cascade (finbert success ->
  finbert-unavailable + vader success -> both-unavailable + keyword
  fallback) is exercised by patching the transformers.pipeline /
  vaderSentiment imports directly, since real model downloads require
  network access unavailable in this sandbox; one test also confirms
  the actual real-environment behavior (network-less sandbox falls
  through to vader).
- score()'s dispatch logic, truncation, and exception-swallowing are
  tested with MagicMock doubles for _pipeline/_vader set directly on
  the instance (duck-typing instead of loading real ML models).
- _score_finbert/_score_vader/_score_keyword are each tested directly
  with concrete inputs (positive/negative-dominant, confidence
  capping, no-keyword-match neutral case).
- classify_event()'s crisis/macro/regulatory/score-based branches
  (incl. crisis-pattern-takes-priority-over-macro) are tested with
  real regex-matching text, no mocking needed.
- No production code changes. Full suite verified green: 1210
  passed, 9 skipped, 0 failed. Coverage 93.07% -> 93.42%. ruff
  unchanged (22, pre-existing). mypy sgr/ unchanged (118,
  pre-existing).
